            <div xml:id="d1453">

                <pb facs="1224" n="1120" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.55/22.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister to China.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-09-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 19, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Legation at Panama reports that the Government of Panama on the 17th instant
                    revoked the exequatur of the Chinese Consul General on the ground of encouraging
                    the Chinese not to comply with the law requiring registration of Chinese. The
                    Legation states that although the period of registration expired September 15
                    without the Chinese complying with the law, the Government of Panama has not
                    applied coercive measures. Chinese Chargé d’Affaires here advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
